          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "しんようする — shin'yō suru — \"to trust; to believe in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "うそを 言ったので、かれを しんようしません。 — uso o itta node, kare o shin'yō shimasen — \"He lied, so I don't trust him.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite しんようします, shin'yōshimasu; a する verb. Past (polite): みんなが かれを しんようしました。, minna ga kare o shin'yō shimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "しんようする (shin'yō suru) is built from a Sino-Japanese noun and the native verb suru, \"to do\". The noun, shin'yō, is two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese: shin, \"trust\" (Middle Chinese sinH) and yō, \"utilize\" (yowngH) (KANJIDIC2; JMdict; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
